WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.834 --> 00:00:03.135
-President Trump's firing

00:00:03.135 --> 00:00:04.771
of former Veterans Affairs
Secretary David Shulkin

00:00:04.771 --> 00:00:07.073
last month sparked a debate
about whether or not

00:00:07.073 --> 00:00:09.408
Trump will move to privatize
the VA.

00:00:09.408 --> 00:00:11.444
So how concerned should we be,

00:00:11.444 --> 00:00:13.646
and has Trump made good
on his promise

00:00:13.646 --> 00:00:15.148
to fix the VA in general?

00:00:15.148 --> 00:00:16.916
It's time for "The Check In."

00:00:16.916 --> 00:00:18.818
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:18.818 --> 00:00:20.553
[ Bell dings ]

00:00:20.553 --> 00:00:24.224
-President Trump has an idea
how to fix some of the problems

00:00:24.224 --> 00:00:26.559
with the Department of Veterans
Affairs healthcare system.

00:00:26.559 --> 00:00:28.327
See if you can spot the one word

00:00:28.327 --> 00:00:30.263
he thinks will make
all the difference.

00:00:30.263 --> 00:00:33.199
-We're going to have a choice.
And we are now doing choice.

00:00:33.199 --> 00:00:37.036
We are going to ensure every
veteran in America

00:00:37.036 --> 00:00:41.775
has the choice to seek care
at the Veterans Administration

00:00:41.775 --> 00:00:45.078
or to seek private medical care.

00:00:45.078 --> 00:00:46.746
We want them to have choice.

00:00:46.746 --> 00:00:49.615
-"Choice" is the word
Republicans use

00:00:49.615 --> 00:00:51.050
when they mean privatization,

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.686
because there's this mind-set
on the right

00:00:53.686 --> 00:00:55.521
that the private sector
can do everything

00:00:55.521 --> 00:00:56.822
better than the government can.

00:00:56.822 --> 00:00:58.658
There is debate to be had,
but I'll just say

00:00:58.658 --> 00:01:01.894
that the Hoover Dam has been
there for almost 90 years,

00:01:01.894 --> 00:01:04.664
while the Jamba Juice on your
block that used to be a Curves

00:01:04.664 --> 00:01:05.798
is now a Chipotle.

00:01:05.798 --> 00:01:07.633
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:07.633 --> 00:01:09.536
Trump talks about this idea
of choice

00:01:09.536 --> 00:01:11.304
like he came up with it,
but in reality,

00:01:11.304 --> 00:01:13.539
The Veterans Access, Choice,
and Accountability Act

00:01:13.539 --> 00:01:15.574
has been in place since 2014 --

00:01:15.574 --> 00:01:18.311
You know, back when your
Chipotle was a RadioShack.

00:01:18.311 --> 00:01:19.378
[ Laughter ]

00:01:19.378 --> 00:01:20.813
Now, among other things,

00:01:20.813 --> 00:01:23.549
the act allows veterans
to seek private care

00:01:23.549 --> 00:01:26.152
if they live too far
from the VA facility

00:01:26.152 --> 00:01:28.587
or have to wait too long
to get an appointment.

00:01:28.587 --> 00:01:29.989
But even with that choice,

00:01:29.989 --> 00:01:32.625
studies have shown that veterans
overwhelmingly prefer

00:01:32.625 --> 00:01:33.959
to go to the VA for their care.

00:01:33.959 --> 00:01:36.129
But, unfortunately,
when it comes to decisions

00:01:36.129 --> 00:01:38.063
involving veterans,
Trump reportedly

00:01:38.063 --> 00:01:41.568
seeks the advice of Fox News
personality and Iraq war veteran

00:01:41.568 --> 00:01:44.570
Pete Hegseth,
who favors an overhaul of the VA

00:01:44.570 --> 00:01:45.805
and who was on
Trump's short list

00:01:45.805 --> 00:01:47.840
to be the next
Secretary of Veterans Affairs.

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:50.243
Now, you might be
unfamiliar with Hegseth

00:01:50.243 --> 00:01:52.011
because you don't watch Fox News

00:01:52.011 --> 00:01:53.947
or you're very familiar
with him,

00:01:53.947 --> 00:01:55.948
which means you just
hate watching my show,

00:01:55.948 --> 00:01:57.383
and, frankly,
I don't appreciate that.

00:01:57.383 --> 00:01:59.152
[ Laughter ]

00:01:59.152 --> 00:02:00.486
So to get you better acquainted,

00:02:00.486 --> 00:02:03.389
here he is weighing in on issues
raging from the NFL

00:02:03.389 --> 00:02:05.625
to Charlottesville to
the March For Our Lives.

00:02:05.625 --> 00:02:06.559
-I have to ask you, what are

00:02:06.559 --> 00:02:07.627
we kneeling for at this point,

00:02:07.627 --> 00:02:09.094
because you talk about
social injustice.

00:02:09.094 --> 00:02:10.763
This is the least sexist,

00:02:10.763 --> 00:02:12.866
least racist, most free,

00:02:12.866 --> 00:02:14.533
most equal, most prosperous

00:02:14.533 --> 00:02:15.768
country in the history

00:02:15.768 --> 00:02:17.770
of human -- human kind.

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:19.205
I think the president nailed it,

00:02:19.205 --> 00:02:21.274
condemn in the strongest
possible terms

00:02:21.274 --> 00:02:23.475
hatred and bigotry, on all sides

00:02:23.475 --> 00:02:24.811
as opposed to immediately

00:02:24.811 --> 00:02:26.245
picking a side out the gate.

00:02:26.245 --> 00:02:28.114
Forgive me if I don't want
a lesson on the Second Amendment

00:02:28.114 --> 00:02:29.315
from a 16-year-old.

00:02:29.315 --> 00:02:30.283
Forgive me if I don't want watch

00:02:30.283 --> 00:02:31.450
a 9-year-old tell me that her

00:02:31.450 --> 00:02:32.919
dream is a world without guns.

00:02:32.919 --> 00:02:33.819
I watched that and you know

00:02:33.819 --> 00:02:34.887
what my reaction was, honestly?

00:02:34.887 --> 00:02:36.356
I donated to the NRA
this morning.

00:02:36.356 --> 00:02:38.390
I'm serious.

00:02:38.390 --> 00:02:40.259
-No one thinks
you're not serious.

00:02:40.259 --> 00:02:41.427
[ Laughter ]

00:02:41.427 --> 00:02:42.895
But here's where I'm serious.

00:02:42.895 --> 00:02:45.764
I hope you're better with a gun
than you are with an axe.

00:02:45.764 --> 00:02:48.768
This is an actual clip
of Pete Hegseth.

00:02:48.768 --> 00:02:50.002
-Plus, Pete and Clayton

00:02:50.002 --> 00:02:51.070
are facing off.

00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:52.772
They're testing their skills

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:53.940
with the axe.

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:55.107
Who's going to win this battle

00:02:55.107 --> 00:02:56.742
of the lumberjacks?

00:02:56.742 --> 00:02:58.811
[ Audience gasps, murmuring ]

00:02:58.811 --> 00:03:00.813
I'm putting my money on...

00:03:00.813 --> 00:03:02.148
Clayton.

00:03:02.148 --> 00:03:03.749
-It's like the saying goes --

00:03:03.749 --> 00:03:07.420
the only thing that stops a bad
guy with an axe is a drum kit?

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:08.888
[ Laughter ]

00:03:08.888 --> 00:03:11.390
Now, both Hegseth
and the White House deny

00:03:11.390 --> 00:03:13.192
that Trump's wanting to
privatize the VA,

00:03:13.192 --> 00:03:15.161
but it's difficult to take
that argument seriously

00:03:15.161 --> 00:03:17.363
because Trump floated the idea
of privatization

00:03:17.363 --> 00:03:19.031
shortly after he was elected.

00:03:19.031 --> 00:03:20.500
If the VA were privatized,

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:22.935
it would only benefit a select
few, like big hospitals

00:03:22.935 --> 00:03:25.171
and providers
at the expense of taxpayers

00:03:25.171 --> 00:03:27.139
and veterans themselves,
and these concerns

00:03:27.139 --> 00:03:29.708
were heightened after
Trump's former VA Secretary

00:03:29.708 --> 00:03:32.878
David Shulkin said he was fired
because he refused to go along

00:03:32.878 --> 00:03:34.480
with privatizing the VA.

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:36.082
-Shulkin alleged today he was

00:03:36.082 --> 00:03:37.650
fired because he did not want to

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:39.752
privatize VA care, in essence,

00:03:39.752 --> 00:03:42.155
because he refused
to dismantle the VA.

00:03:42.155 --> 00:03:43.555
He claims he fell victim to

00:03:43.555 --> 00:03:46.292
a power play by Trump's
political appointees.

00:03:49.562 --> 00:03:52.131
-The good news for Shulkin
is every time Trump removes

00:03:52.131 --> 00:03:55.501
an obstacle, it comes back
as an even bigger obstacle.

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:57.837
Trump removed James Comey,
Comey wrote a book.

00:03:57.837 --> 00:03:59.906
Trump removed Michael Flynn,
Flynn flipped.

00:03:59.906 --> 00:04:01.373
If Trump had a mole removed,

00:04:01.373 --> 00:04:03.643
it would be testifying before
Congress a week later.

00:04:03.643 --> 00:04:05.044
[ Laughter ]

00:04:05.044 --> 00:04:07.112
Now Trump could have chosen
a number of qualified people

00:04:07.112 --> 00:04:08.581
to replace David Shulkin
at the VA.

00:04:08.581 --> 00:04:10.850
Someone who has experience
running a massive bureaucracy

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:12.118
would have been a good start.

00:04:12.118 --> 00:04:14.086
But instead, Trump went
with White House doctor

00:04:14.086 --> 00:04:16.522
and Navy Rear Admiral
Dr. Ronny Jackson.

00:04:16.522 --> 00:04:19.091
That's right, he chose
the White House doctor.

00:04:19.091 --> 00:04:20.292
I guess we should
just be happy

00:04:20.292 --> 00:04:22.028
Trump didn't go with
his personal doctor.

00:04:22.028 --> 00:04:24.564
In case you don't remember...
[ Laughter ]

00:04:24.564 --> 00:04:27.333
That is, for real,
Trump's personal doctor

00:04:27.333 --> 00:04:28.801
Harold Bornstein.

00:04:28.801 --> 00:04:31.604
Aw, bro.

00:04:31.604 --> 00:04:35.207
Brooooo.

00:04:35.207 --> 00:04:36.976
You got a little PTSD?

00:04:36.976 --> 00:04:38.711
You need a little
hydroponic chronic

00:04:38.711 --> 00:04:40.947
and 200cc of Pink Floyd, baby.

00:04:40.947 --> 00:04:42.715
[ Laughter ]

00:04:42.715 --> 00:04:44.917
Now Jackson's hearing,
during which he was expected

00:04:44.917 --> 00:04:46.652
to answer questions about
privatization,

00:04:46.652 --> 00:04:49.321
was set for this Wednesday,
but lawmakers have postponed it

00:04:49.321 --> 00:04:51.723
after they had received
reports of allegations

00:04:51.723 --> 00:04:53.926
that Jackson oversaw
a hostile work environment

00:04:53.926 --> 00:04:54.960
as the White House doctor,

00:04:54.960 --> 00:04:56.929
allowing the overprescribing
of drugs,

00:04:56.929 --> 00:04:59.198
as well as claims
that Dr. Ronny L. Jackson

00:04:59.198 --> 00:05:00.866
drank too much on the job.

00:05:00.866 --> 00:05:03.569
And I for one am shocked
to hear that a 50-year-old man

00:05:03.569 --> 00:05:05.872
who goes by Ronny
would behave improperly.

00:05:05.872 --> 00:05:06.638
[ Laughter ]

00:05:06.638 --> 00:05:08.308
The only way it's okay

00:05:08.308 --> 00:05:09.842
to be a 50-year-old man
named Ronny

00:05:09.842 --> 00:05:11.544
is if you play the jazz flute.

00:05:11.544 --> 00:05:12.712
[ Laughter ]

00:05:12.712 --> 00:05:16.249
Oh, yeah! Dr. Ronny
is in the pocket tonight!

00:05:16.249 --> 00:05:19.651
[ Applause ]

00:05:19.651 --> 00:05:22.788
Now, Trump was asked about
what he thinks Dr. Jackson

00:05:22.788 --> 00:05:24.623
should do next in light
of these allegations.

00:05:24.623 --> 00:05:27.860
And his response was, as usual,
all over the place.

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:30.396
-I said to Dr. Jackson,

00:05:30.396 --> 00:05:31.697
"What do you need it for?"

00:05:31.697 --> 00:05:33.832
So, we'll see what happens.

00:05:33.832 --> 00:05:36.201
I don't want to put
a man through

00:05:36.201 --> 00:05:38.904
who's not a political person --

00:05:38.904 --> 00:05:40.440
I don't want to put a man

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:41.907
through a process like this.

00:05:41.907 --> 00:05:43.943
It's too ugly
and too disgusting.

00:05:43.943 --> 00:05:46.212
If I were him, actually,

00:05:46.212 --> 00:05:48.247
in many ways I'd love to be him,

00:05:48.247 --> 00:05:50.249
but the fact is
I wouldn't do it.

00:05:50.249 --> 00:05:51.617
I wouldn't do it.

00:05:51.617 --> 00:05:53.919
-What do you mean if you were
him, you wouldn't do it?

00:05:53.919 --> 00:05:56.588
You're even less qualified,
and you did do it.

00:05:56.588 --> 00:05:57.823
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:57.823 --> 00:05:59.391
This has been "The Check In."

00:05:59.391 --> 00:06:01.160 line:0%
♪♪

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:02.695
[ Bell dings ]

